    "
  >
    Spotlight
  </h2>
</mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;" color="#000000">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 2px !important;">
    Mexico blames the US
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="Mexico blames the US"
  href="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/"
/>
<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>What’s happening?</strong> Mexican President Claudia Sheinbaum called on the US to <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/09/mexican-cartels-guns-come-from-us-sheinbaum-trump" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">halt the illegal trafficking of firearms</a> into Mexico, responding to President Trump's description of her country as the "epicenter of cartel violence." Sheinbaum argued that cartel violence in Mexico is heavily fueled by weapons smuggled from the US, noting that about 75% of guns used by criminal groups originate there.  She rejected any possibility of US military involvement in Mexico.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Trump’s comments:</strong> Trump argued that Mexican drug cartels were responsible for widespread bloodshed and instability across the region. Trump also claimed he had offered to help Mexico eradicate the cartels with stronger US measures. In his remarks, he referred to President Claudia Sheinbaum as a “beautiful woman” with a “beautiful voice,” comments that critics in Mexico described as inappropriate.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>History:</strong> Mexicans are wary of US interventions, having lost half their national territory to the US in a 1846-48 war that two US presidents, Abraham Lincoln and Ulysses Grant, said was waged under false pretenses to conquer territory and expand slavery. The US also invaded and briefly occupied the port city of Veracruz in 1914 and launched a punitive invasion targeting the revolutionary Pancho Villa’s forces in 1916-17.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

<mj-spacer height="10px" />
